## reading
# * every query command ran against the file+directory read-only store; store.db sha256 unchanged (beee7d57...0b50) and no -wal/-shm
#   was created; no command failed for want of write access (write-error-lines=0 everywhere).
# * exact_grep exit=3 is NOT a write failure: `exact grep --ref product` passes the view ref NAME straight to git ("unable to resolve
#   revision: product"), an unhandled GitError -> INT-D14 (exact path/id map the same name through the view).
# * answers_lint exit=1 is the command's documented "open findings" exit (4 findings on a deliberately flawed synthetic answers file).
# * compile (CONTROL-A, no seeds) on the read-only store is byte-identical to the writable-store compiles (diff -r IDENTICAL above).
# * BUT a SEEDED compile silently differs between the writable and the read-only store: section C loses its graph neighbour
#   (int-08b-seeded-compile-readonly.out; INT-D03) -- the only query-path write left (compile/packet.py storemod.open_db() + traverse.py
#   ensure_schema), swallowed by `except Exception: neighbours = {}`.
